  "text": "```verilog\n`timescale 1ns/1ps\n\nmodule axis_register #\n(\n    parameter DATA_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter KEEP_ENABLE = (DATA_WIDTH>8),\n    parameter KEEP_WIDTH = ((DATA_WIDTH+7)/8),\n    parameter LAST_ENABLE = 1,\n    parameter ID_ENABLE = 0,\n    parameter ID_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter DEST_ENABLE = 0,\n    parameter DEST_WIDTH = 8,\n    parameter USER_ENABLE = 1,\n    parameter USER_WIDTH = 1,\n    parameter REG_TYPE = 2\n)\n(\n    input  wire                   clk,\n    input  wire                   rst,\n    /*\n     * AXI Stream input\n     */\n    input  wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tdata,\n    input  wire [KEEP_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tkeep,\n    input  wire                   s_axis_tvalid,\n    output wire                   s_axis_tready,\n    input  wire                   s_axis_tlast,\n    input  wire [ID_WIDTH-1:0]    s_axis_tid,\n    input  wire [DEST_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tdest,\n    input  wire [USER_WIDTH-1:0]  s_axis_tuser,\n    /*\n     * AXI Stream output\n     */\n    output wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tdata,\n    output wire [KEEP_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tkeep,\n    output wire                   m_axis_tvalid,\n    input  wire                   m_axis_tready,\n    output wire                   m_axis_tlast,\n    output wire [ID_WIDTH-1:0]    m_axis_tid,\n    output wire [DEST_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tdest,\n    output wire [USER_WIDTH-1:0]  m_axis_tuser\n);\n\n    // Internal state registers\n    reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg_data;\n    reg [KEEP_WIDTH-1:0] reg_keep;\n    reg reg_last;\n    reg [ID_WIDTH-1:0]   reg_id;\n    reg [DEST_WIDTH-1:0] reg_dest;\n    reg [USER_WIDTH-1:0] reg_user;\n    reg reg_valid;\n\n    // Control signals\n    wire wire_type;\n    wire wire_buffer;\n    wire wire_skid;\n\n    // Determine register type behavior\n    // REG_TYPE = 0: Wire (Transparent)\n    // REG_TYPE = 1: Buffer (Valid/Ready handshake only)\n    // REG_TYPE = 2: Skid Buffer (Store data on valid, forward on ready)\n    assign wire_type = (REG_TYPE == 0);\n    assign wire_buffer = (REG_TYPE == 1);\n    assign wire_skid = (REG_TYPE == 2);\n\n    // Logic to determine if we should accept new data\n    // For Wire: Always accept if ready\n    // For Buffer: Accept if ready (no storage needed beyond current cycle)\n    // For Skid: Accept if valid and ready (store in register)\n    \n    wire accept_data;\n    assign accept_data = (s_axis_tvalid && m_axis_tready);\n\n    // Logic to determine if we should forward data\n    // For Wire: Forward immediately if valid\n    // For Buffer: Forward immediately if valid\n    // For Skid: Forward if valid and ready (data is already stored)\n    \n    wire forward_data;\n    assign forward_data = (reg_valid && m_axis_tready);\n\n    // State Machine / Logic for each register type\n\n    // 1. Wire Mode (Transparent)\n    // Data passes through immediately. No storage required.\n    // However, to strictly follow \"single-clock\" and \"register slice\" semantics \n    // while acting as a wire, we typically just pass signals. \n    // But the prompt asks for a \"register slice\" that behaves as a wire.\n    // In AXI-Stream, a wire is often implemented by just passing signals, \n    // but if we must use registers to align phases or handle resets cleanly:\n    // We will store data on valid/ready and forward on next clock if ready.\n    // Actually, a true wire is combinational. A \"register wire\" usually implies \n    // storing the data for one cycle. Let's implement the storage logic \n    // but only forward if the downstream is ready.\n    \n    // 2. Buffer Mode\n    // Acts as a buffer. Stores data on valid/ready. \n    // If downstream is not ready, it holds the data.\n    // If downstream is ready, it forwards.\n    // This is effectively the same as Skid but without the \"skid\" delay concept \n    // (i.e., it doesn't necessarily delay the first packet if the first packet \n    // is ready immediately, but it ensures alignment).\n    // Standard interpretation: Buffer stores data when s_valid=1 and m_ready=1.\n    // If m_ready=0, it waits.\n    \n    // 3. Skid Buffer Mode\n    // Stores data on s_valid=1 regardless of m_ready.\n    // Forwards data on m_ready=1.\n    // This decouples the producer and consumer completely.\n\n    // Unified Logic for Data Storage\n    // We store data if:\n    // - Wire: s_valid && m_ready (Transparent pass-through with 1-cycle latency)\n    // - Buffer: s_valid && m_ready (Store if ready, else wait)\n    // - Skid: s_valid (Always store on valid, forward on ready)\n    \n    // Let's refine the \"Buffer\" definition based on standard AXI-Stream implementations.\n    // Often \"Buffer\" means it absorbs a burst if the downstream is slow, \n    // but forwards as soon as possible. \n    // \"Skid\" means it always absorbs one cycle of latency.\n    \n    // Implementation Strategy:\n    // We will use a single set of registers.\n    // The update logic depends on REG_TYPE.\n    \n    // Update Logic\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin\n        if (rst) begin\n            reg_data      <= 0;\n            reg_keep      <= 0;\n            reg_last      <= 0;\n            reg_id        <= 0;\n            reg_dest      <= 0;\n            reg_user      <= 0;\n            reg_valid     <= 0;\n        end else begin\n            // Determine if we update the register\n            wire update_reg;\n            \n            if (wire_skid) begin\n                // Skid Buffer: Update on s_valid, regardless of m_ready\n                update_reg = s_axis_tvalid;\n            end else if (wire_buffer) begin\n                // Buffer: Update on s_valid && m_ready\n                // If m_ready is 0, we don't update (we wait for the next cycle where m_ready might be 1)\n                // This creates a \"buffer\" effect where we only commit when the path is clear.\n                update_reg = (s_axis_tvalid && m_axis_tready);\n            end else begin\n                // Wire: Update on s_valid && m_ready (1-cycle latency wire)\n                update_reg = (s_axis_tvalid && m_axis_tready);\n            end\n\n            if (update_reg) begin\n                reg_data      <= s_axis_tdata;\n                reg_keep      <= s_axis_tkeep;\n                reg_last      <= s_axis_tlast;\n                reg_id        <= s_axis_tid;\n                reg_dest      <= s_axis_tdest;\n                reg_user      <= s_axis_tuser;\n                reg_valid     <= 1;\n            end else begin\n                // For Skid, if we don't update, we must clear valid if s_valid was 0\n                // For Wire/Buffer, if we don't update, valid should be 0\n                if (wire_skid) begin\n                    // In skid mode, if s_valid is 0, we must clear the register\n                    if (!s_axis_tvalid) begin\n                        reg_valid <= 0;\n                    end\n                    // If s_valid is 1 but m_ready is 0, we keep the data (already handled by update_reg logic)\n                end else begin\n                    // Wire/Buffer: If we didn't update, it means we didn't get a valid/ready pair\n                    // So valid becomes 0\n                    reg_valid <= 0;\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Output Logic\n    // Determine when to assert m_valid\n    // Wire/Buffer: m_valid = reg_valid && m_axis_tready\n    // Skid: m_valid = reg_valid && m_axis_tready (Same logic, but data is always present)\n    \n    always @(*) begin\n        m_axis_tvalid = (reg_valid && m_axis_tready);\n        \n        if (m_axis_tvalid) begin\n            m_axis_tdata      = reg_data;\n            m_axis_tkeep      = reg_keep;\n            m_axis_tlast      = reg_last;\n            m_axis_tid        = reg_id;\n            m_axis_tdest      = reg_dest;\n            m_axis_tuser      = reg_user;\n        end else begin\n            m_axis_tdata      = 0;\n            m_axis_tkeep      = 0;\n            m_axis_tlast      = 0;\n            m_axis_tid        = 0;\n            m_axis_tdest      = 0;\n            m_axis_tuser      = 0;\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Input Ready Logic\n    // s_axis_tready is asserted if we are ready to accept data.\n    // Wire/Buffer: Ready if m_axis_tready is 1 (and we are not in a state where we are waiting for m_ready to update)\n    // Actually, for Wire/Buffer:\n    // If REG_TYPE != Skid:\n    //   We need s_valid && m_ready to update.\n    //   So s_ready = m_ready.\n    // If REG_TYPE == Skid:\n    //   We update on s_valid.\n    //   So s_ready = 1 (always ready to accept).\n    \n    assign s_axis_tready = (wire_skid) ? 1'b1 : m_axis_tready;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
